[h2]0.2[/h2]
[list]
[*] [b]A generic map tack can now be placed on coast, navigable river and mountain.[/b] Detailed Map Tacks refuses those tiles for a generic tack because it can only check terrain for a named building - but 12 buildings belong on water (Lighthouse, Port, Wharf, Shipyard, Fishing Quay, Harbor, the bridges, coastal walls), along with three wonders, two improvements, and Machu Picchu on a mountain. A generic tack now answers "could something of this kind stand here".
[*] [b]The Influence tack finally shows example buildings, and they follow the age.[/b] Every other generic tack lists a couple of examples in its tooltip - Production shows Barracks and Blacksmith - but Influence showed none, because that tack has no adjacency rules for the host to read. The list now comes from what actually pays Influence: Monument and Villa in Antiquity, Dungeon and Guildhall in Exploration, Opera House and Radio Station in Modern. (Arena is not one of them - it pays Happiness and Gold.)
[/list]

[h2]0.1[/h2]
[b]First release.[/b] An add-on for [b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] by wltk - it builds on that mod and does nothing without it. Two optional changes, both switchable:
[list]
[*] [b]A generic map tack now disappears once something that fulfils it is built.[/b] Detailed Map Tacks clears a tack when the building it names is finished on that tile, but the check compares the two type names as text - so only a tack for one specific building ever matched. A "culture building" or "wonder" tack has no single name to match and stayed on the map. It now clears as soon as a building that fulfils it goes up, using the same list of buildings the tack's own tooltip shows you.
[*] [b]Right-click a map tack on the map to delete it.[/b] On its own, Detailed Map Tacks deletes a tack on left-click and only while the tack chooser is open. The click is swallowed, so it does not also send your selected unit walking to that tile.
[*] Walls and other slotless buildings do not clear a tack, and a unique quarter tack waits for both of its buildings - a plan is only cleared when it is actually finished.
[*] Both options live under a [b]Detailed Map Tacks[/b] heading in Options - Mods. [b]Apply Najane's changes[/b] and [b]Remove map tacks with right-click[/b] are both on by default.
[*] Requires Detailed Map Tacks, declared as a hard dependency, so nothing applies if that mod is missing or switched off.
[*] Available in twelve languages.
[/list]
[b]wltk:[/b] these are suggestions, not corrections. If you want either change in Detailed Map Tacks itself, take it - the source is at [url=https://github.com/bopielka/detailed-map-tacks-fixes]github.com/bopielka/detailed-map-tacks-fixes[/url], no attribution needed.
